WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.802
Friday, 4:40.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.633
The client wants a proposal
by Monday, and on the call,

00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:08.654
they asked for a launch discount.

00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:12.926
The account lead types
12% into the proposal.

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:16.038
The price comes from a
rate card spreadsheet.

00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:19.358
The costs live in a
file they can't open.

00:00:19.904 --> 00:00:23.329
And approval is a message
to a partner on a train.

00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:25.047
"Can I do 12?"

00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:26.208
Fine.

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:30.179
Nobody works out what
12% does to the margin.

00:00:30.585 --> 00:00:35.112
It takes a £50,000
job from 39% to 30%.

00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:38.259
Five points under the firm's floor.

00:00:38.897 --> 00:00:43.553
And it goes out without the one person
allowed to approve it ever seeing

00:00:43.611 --> 00:00:44.389
that number.

00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:48.417
This is Proposal and Quote Agent.

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:49.996
Start with the brief.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:55.046
It turns the call and the client's
emails into a list of requirements,

00:00:55.232 --> 00:00:57.067
each with the words that support it.

00:00:57.705 --> 00:01:01.676
Where the client contradicts
themselves, a hard stop in November,

00:01:02.024 --> 00:01:07.051
a phased rollout into next year, it drafts
the question instead of picking one.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.650
Then it builds the price
from your own rate card.

00:01:11.382 --> 00:01:12.485
Four disciplines.

00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:14.215
62 days.

00:01:14.609 --> 00:01:16.978
£50,200.

00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:19.102
Now move the discount.

00:01:19.636 --> 00:01:23.514
At 12%, the margin turns
red, and the proposal

00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:26.498
routes itself to the founding partner.

00:01:27.032 --> 00:01:30.376
Drop to 5%, and the
margin clears the floor.

00:01:30.724 --> 00:01:31.955
It's ready to send.

00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:38.108
Try 6%, and it notices that
34.6% is still under 35%.

00:01:38.573 --> 00:01:40.569
The client pushes for 15%.

00:01:40.976 --> 00:01:44.006
So the partner sees the
margin, and approves it.

00:01:44.645 --> 00:01:46.943
Once it's sent, the price locks.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:54.571
The preview, the follow-up and
the pipeline all say £42,670.

00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:59.447
So every proposal leaves at a
price someone with authority chose,

00:01:59.796 --> 00:02:02.187
knowing exactly what
it costs the firm.

00:02:02.907 --> 00:02:05.090
The discount is a decision.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:06.820
Never a slip.
